{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "```python\nclass Number:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates number operations like digit reversal and arithmetic calculation.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: int):\n        self.value = value\n\n    def reverse_digits(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Reverses the digits of the stored number, ignoring its sign.\"\"\"\n        return int(str(abs(self.value))[::-1])\n\n    def calculate_twice_reversed_minus_one(self, reversed_num: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the target value: (2 * reversed_num) - 1.\"\"\"\n        return (2 * reversed_num) - 1\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def is_one_less_than_twice_reverse(original: int, calculated: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Compares the original number with the calculated target value.\"\"\"\n        return original == calculated\n\ndef check(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number is one less than twice its reverse.\n    This function orchestrates the Number class to perform the necessary computations.\n    \"\"\"\n    number_obj = Number(number)\n    reversed_num = number_obj.reverse_digits()\n    calculated_value = number_obj.calculate_twice_reversed_minus_one(reversed_num)\n\n    return Number.is_one_less_than_twice_reverse(number, calculated_value)\n```"}
