{"task_id": "Mbpp/57", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Max_Num(digits: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Forms the largest possible number from a given list of digits.\n    The function converts digits to strings and sorts them using custom comparison.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not digits:\n        return 0\n\n    str_digits = [str(d) for d in digits]\n\n    n = len(str_digits)\n    # Perform a bubble sort with custom comparison logic.\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        for j in range(n - 1 - i):\n            # If placing str_digits[j+1] before str_digits[j] forms a larger number, swap them.\n            if int(str_digits[j] + str_digits[j+1]) < int(str_digits[j+1] + str_digits[j]):\n                str_digits[j], str_digits[j+1] = str_digits[j+1], str_digits[j]\n\n    # Join the sorted digit strings and convert to an integer.\n    largest_num_str = \"\".join(str_digits)\n    return int(largest_num_str)\n```"}
